WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:05.600 --> 00:00:08.960
How air conditioning works.

00:00:11.200 --> 00:00:16.860
There are eight main components that
play a pivotal role in cooling your home.

00:00:17.060 --> 00:00:18.660
A Thermostat

00:00:19.000 --> 00:00:20.520
Condenser

00:00:20.800 --> 00:00:22.340
Compressor

00:00:22.560 --> 00:00:24.000
Fan

00:00:24.240 --> 00:00:25.960
Metering Device

00:00:26.260 --> 00:00:27.640
Evaporator

00:00:27.820 --> 00:00:29.120
Blower

00:00:29.340 --> 00:00:31.080
and a Filter.

00:00:32.480 --> 00:00:38.100
The first step begins with setting your
thermostat to the desired temperature.

00:00:38.800 --> 00:00:43.000
This triggers the condenser fan and
compressor to turn on.

00:00:43.440 --> 00:00:48.000
The compressor begins pumping a fluid
called a 'refrigerant' throughout the system.

00:00:48.380 --> 00:00:51.440
This is used because of its low boiling point.

00:00:52.380 --> 00:00:54.400
Refrigerant constantly changes from a

00:00:54.400 --> 00:00:57.120
vapor to a liquid in order to move heat from

00:00:57.120 --> 00:00:59.460
inside your home to the outdoors.

00:01:00.860 --> 00:01:05.080
It enters the compressor as a low-temperature, low-pressure vapor.

00:01:05.560 --> 00:01:10.760
After it's compressed, it leaves as a high-temperature, high-pressure vapor.

00:01:14.000 --> 00:01:19.040
It then travels through the condenser
coil, where the vapor condenses into a liquid.

00:01:19.040 --> 00:01:23.640
The heat it has collected indoors and after compression, is released outside.

00:01:25.680 --> 00:01:30.260
The fan inside the unit helps with this
process.

00:01:30.880 --> 00:01:36.700
The refrigerant leaves the condenser as
a medium-temperature, high-pressure liquid.

00:01:37.440 --> 00:01:40.760
Then, flows to the metering device.

00:01:41.400 --> 00:01:46.160
In this case, a thermal expansion valve is used.

00:01:46.720 --> 00:01:50.800
A pin inside the valve adjusts the flow rate of refrigerant

00:01:50.800 --> 00:01:56.020
depending on the temperature at the
evaporator end, using a 'sensing bulb'.

00:01:58.160 --> 00:02:02.240
As it flows through the valve, its
pressure drops significantly,

00:02:02.240 --> 00:02:06.640
releasing a low-temperature, low-pressure liquid/vapor mix.

00:02:06.640 --> 00:02:11.660
The lower pressure allows room
temperature air to boil the refrigerant.

00:02:12.080 --> 00:02:17.740
The chilled refrigerant then flows
through the evaporator coil.

00:02:22.640 --> 00:02:27.100
The blower begins circulating air
throughout the house.

00:02:30.160 --> 00:02:33.520
Room-temperature air is pulled in through the return duct

00:02:33.520 --> 00:02:37.360
and passes through the filter to remove particulates.

00:02:37.360 --> 00:02:42.160
The heat from the air is absorbed into
the refrigerant inside the evaporator coil,

00:02:42.160 --> 00:02:45.860
dispersing chilled air through the supply duct.

00:02:46.960 --> 00:02:49.480
As the air passes over the coil,

00:02:49.480 --> 00:02:54.040
the refrigerant is boiled and evaporates back into vapor form.

00:02:55.200 --> 00:02:59.280
During this process, condensation forms on the outside of the coil

00:02:59.280 --> 00:03:02.840
and exits through a condensate drain
line.

00:03:03.520 --> 00:03:08.560
The refrigerant returns to the condenser
to disperse the collected heat outdoors,

00:03:08.560 --> 00:03:11.580
and the cycle starts again.

00:03:17.960 --> 00:03:19.760
Your home is slowly cooled,

00:03:19.760 --> 00:03:22.060
and the thermostat shuts off the equipment

00:03:22.060 --> 00:03:25.480
once it senses the desired temperature.

